\layout Standard

Dans le cas ou l'on prend en compte le type de trajectoire il faut moyenner
 les equations selon la relation 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ \mathcal{A}\right\} =\frac{1}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\xi_{0}}{\xi}\mathcal{A}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

ou 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)=\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\xi_{0}}{\xi}\]

\end_inset 

et 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma=\frac{p_{\Vert}}{\left|p_{\Vert}\right|}$
\end_inset 

est le signe de 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{\Vert}$
\end_inset 

et 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta$
\end_inset 

est l'angle poloidal.Ici 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{c}$
\end_inset 

vaut 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi$
\end_inset 

pour les particules circulantes et 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{T}=$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\cos^{-1}\left(1-2\xi_{0}^{2}/\xi_{0T}^{2}\right)$
\end_inset 

pour les particules piegees, avec 
\begin_inset Formula $\xi_{0T}^{2}=$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\frac{2\varepsilon}{1+\varepsilon},$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon=r/R_{0}$
\end_inset 

etant l'inverse du rapport d'aspect.L'equation de Fokker-Planck moyennee
 devient alors
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ \frac{\partial\left(rp^{2}f_{0}\right)}{\partial t}\right\} +\left\{ r\frac{\partial\left(p^{2}S_{p}\right)}{\partial p}\right\} -\left\{ rp\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\right\} =0\]

\end_inset 

ou le parametre temps 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset 

evolue sur une echelle bien plus longue que la periode de rebond 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\tau_{t,b}=\frac{2\pi R_{0}q\left(r\right)}{\left|\xi_{0}\right|v}\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\]

\end_inset 

On definit ici le facteur de securite 
\begin_inset Formula $q\left(r\right)$
\end_inset 

de la surface de flux magnetique situee au rayon 
\begin_inset Formula $r$
\end_inset 

sur laquelle la moyenne est effectuee et 
\begin_inset Formula $R_{0}$
\end_inset 

le grand rayon du plasma.Toutes les valeurs sont determinees au point ou
 le champ magnetique estminimum, la ou toutes les particules passent, soit
 notamment 
\begin_inset Formula $\xi_{0}$
\end_inset 

pour l'angle de diffusion angulaire et la fonction de distribution 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}$
\end_inset 

.On a ainsi 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ \frac{\partial\left(rp^{2}f_{0}\right)}{\partial t}\right\} =rp^{2}\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\left[\frac{1}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\xi_{0}}{\xi}f_{0}\right]\]

\end_inset 

et comme 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{0}$
\end_inset 

est par definition symetrique en 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta,$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ \frac{\partial\left(rp^{2}f_{0}\right)}{\partial t}\right\} =\frac{\partial\left(rp^{2}f_{0}^{(0)}\right)}{\partial t}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

De maniere evidente 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ r\frac{\partial\left(p^{2}S_{p}\right)}{\partial p}\right\} =r\frac{\partial\left(p^{2}\left\{ S_{p}\right\} \right)}{\partial p}\]

\end_inset 

et pour le second terme de droite il faut utiliser la relation 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi}=$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\xi}{\Psi\xi_{0}}\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}},$
\end_inset 

sachant que 
\begin_inset Formula $\xi=$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\sigma\sqrt{1-\Psi\left(1-\xi_{0}^{2}\right)}$
\end_inset 

avec 
\begin_inset Formula $\Psi\left(r,\theta\right)=\frac{1+\varepsilon}{1+\varepsilon\cos\theta}.$
\end_inset 

Il vient alors 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ rp\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\right\} =\frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\xi_{0}}{\xi}\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\]

\end_inset 

soit apres le changement de variable 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ rp\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\right\} =\frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{1}{\Psi}\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi_{0}}\]

\end_inset 

Afin de permuter la derivee en 
\begin_inset Formula $\xi_{0}$
\end_inset 

et la somme sur 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma$
\end_inset 

pour les particules piegees, il faut introduire 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma$
\end_inset 

, de sorte que 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\{ rp\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\right\}  & = & \frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial\left(\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\sigma}{\Psi}\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\left|\xi_{0}\right|}\\
 & = & \frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial\left(\sigma\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\sigma}{\Psi}\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi_{0}}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

et il est possible d'exprimer le terme dans la derivee partielle 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}$
\end_inset 

sous la forme simple 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sigma\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\right]_{T}\int_{-\theta_{c}}^{\theta_{c}}\frac{d\theta}{2\pi}\frac{\sigma}{\Psi}\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}=\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}S_{\xi}\right\} \]

\end_inset 

ce qui donne 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ rp\frac{\partial\left(\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}S_{\xi}\right)}{\partial\xi}\right\} =\frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}S_{\xi}\right\} \right)}{\partial\xi_{0}}\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

En posant formellement les nouvelles definitions des flux moyennes sousla
 forme de leur valeur ou le champ magnetique 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset 

est minimum, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{(0)}=\left\{ \begin{array}{l}
S_{p}^{(0)}=\left\{ S_{p}\right\} \\
S_{\xi_{0}}^{(0)}=\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}S_{\xi}\right\} \end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 

on peut garder une forme conservative simple pour l'equation de Fokker-Planck
\begin_inset Formula \[
\frac{\partial\left(rp^{2}f_{0}^{(0)}\right)}{\partial t}+r\frac{\partial}{\partial p}(p^{2}S_{p}^{(0)})-\frac{rp}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\left(\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)S_{\xi_{0}}^{(0)}\right)=0\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Il est egalement possible de garder la forme originale pour l'expressiondes
 flux, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
S_{p} & = & -D_{pp}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial p}+D_{p\xi}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}}{p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial\xi}+F_{p}f_{0}\\
S_{\xi} & = & -D_{\xi p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial p}+D_{\xi\xi}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}}{p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial\xi}+F_{\xi}f_{0}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Les moyennes sur la trajectoire des flux definies ci-dessus donnent alors
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\{ -D_{pp}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial p}\right\}  & = & -\left\{ D_{pp}\right\} \frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}\\
\left\{ D_{p\xi}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}}{p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial\xi}\right\}  & = & \frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}}{p}\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{p\xi}\right\} \frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\sigma\partial\xi_{0}}\\
\left\{ F_{p}f_{0}\right\}  & = & \left\{ F_{p}\right\} f_{0}^{(0)}\\
-\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{\xi p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial p}\right\}  & = & -\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{\xi p}\right\} \frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}\\
-\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{\xi\xi}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi^{2}}}{p}\frac{\partial f_{0}}{\partial\xi}\right\}  & = & -\sigma\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}}{p}\left\{ \frac{\xi^{2}}{\Psi\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi\xi}\right\} \frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\sigma\partial\xi_{0}}\\
\sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}F_{\xi}f_{0}\right\}  & = & \sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}F_{\xi}\right\} f_{0}^{(0)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

de sorte que l'on peut reecrire 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{(0)}=-\overline{\overline{D}}_{p}^{(0)}\cdot\nabla_{p,\xi_{0}}f_{0}^{(0)}+\overline{\overline{F}}_{p}^{(0)}f_{0}^{(0)}\]

\end_inset 

avec les elements de la matrice de diffusion 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
D_{pp}^{(0)} & = & \left\{ D_{pp}\right\} \\
D_{p\xi}^{(0)} & = & \sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{p\xi}\right\} \\
D_{\xi p}^{(0)} & = & \sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}D_{\xi p}\right\} \\
D_{\xi\xi}^{(0)} & = & \left\{ \frac{\xi^{2}}{\Psi\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi\xi}\right\} \end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

et les termes de convection 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
F_{p}^{(0)} & = & \left\{ F_{p}\right\} \\
F_{\xi}^{(0)} & = & \sigma\left\{ \frac{\sigma\xi}{\sqrt{\Psi}\xi_{0}}F_{\xi}\right\} \end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Le gradient s'exprime alors suivant 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\nabla_{p,\xi_{0}}=\left\{ \begin{array}{l}
\nabla_{p}=\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\\
\nabla_{\xi_{0}}=-\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}}{p}\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Les composantes du flux moyenne sur la periode de rebond dans l'espace desimpuls
ions valent donc 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{(0)}=\left\{ \begin{array}{l}
S_{p}^{(0)}=-D_{pp}^{(0)}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}+\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}}{p}D_{p\xi}^{(0)}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}+F_{p}^{(0)}f_{0}^{(0)}\\
S_{\xi_{0}}^{(0)}=-D_{\xi p}^{(0)}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}+\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}}{p}D_{\xi\xi}^{(0)}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}+F_{\xi}^{(0)}f_{0}^{(0)}\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

L'equation de flux devient alors 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\frac{\partial\left(p^{2}S_{p}^{(0)}\right)}{\partial p} & = & \frac{\partial}{\partial p}\left(-p^{2}D_{pp}^{(0)}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}+p^{2}F_{p}^{(0)}f_{0}^{(0)}\right)\\
 &  & +\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}\frac{\partial}{\partial p}\left(pD_{p\xi}^{(0)}\right)\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}+\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}pD_{p\xi}^{(0)}\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p\partial\xi_{0}}\\
\frac{1}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}S_{\xi}^{(0)}\right)}{\partial\xi_{0}} & = & \frac{1}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)D_{\xi\xi}^{(0)}\frac{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}{p}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}+\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}F_{\xi}f_{0}^{(0)}\right)\\
 &  & -\frac{1}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)}\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi p}^{(0)}\right)\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial p}-\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi p}^{(0)}\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial\xi_{0}\partial p}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

En discretisant, puis en les regroupant comme dans le cas non-moyenne, onobtient
 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
 &  & r_{l+1/2}p_{i+1/2}^{2}\frac{f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k)}}{\Delta t}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{-p_{i+1}^{2}D_{pp,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1}^{2}F_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}f_{0,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{p_{i}^{2}D_{pp,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}-p_{i}^{2}F_{p,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}f_{0,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}p_{i+1/2}D_{p\xi,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p\partial\xi_{0}}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}\left.\frac{\partial\left(pD_{p\xi}^{\left(0\right)}\right)}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -r_{l+1/2}\frac{D_{\xi\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\left(1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}F_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{D_{\xi\xi,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}\left(1-\xi_{0j}^{2}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\xi_{0}}\right|_{i+1/2,j}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j}^{2}}F_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}f_{0,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}p_{i+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\xi_{0}\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}p_{i+1/2}\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi p}^{\left(0\right)}\right)\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 & = & 0\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

ou l'indice 
\begin_inset Formula $(k)$
\end_inset 

indique que la variable est prise au temps 
\begin_inset Formula $t=k\Delta t,$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t$
\end_inset 

etant le pas de temps.Le terme de droite est pris au temps 
\begin_inset Formula $(k+1)$
\end_inset 

, ce qui correspond a un schema totalement implicite ou temps inverse, inconditi
onnellement stable numeriquement, point qui sera rediscute dans un chapitresuiva
nt.On discretise egalement 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p\partial\xi_{0}}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)} & = & \left.\frac{\partial^{2}f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\xi_{0}\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 & = & \frac{f_{0,i+3/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i+3/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i-1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}+f_{0,i-1/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\left(\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}\right)\left(\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

tandis que 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial\left(pD_{p\xi}^{\left(0\right)}\right)}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2} & = & \frac{p_{i+1}D_{p\xi,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}-p_{i}D_{p\xi,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial\xi_{0}}\left(\lambda\left(\xi_{0}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0}^{2}}D_{\xi p}^{\left(0\right)}\right)\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2} & = & \frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}-\lambda\left(\xi_{0j}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j}^{2}}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

L'equation de Fokker-Planck moyennee sur la periode de rebond devient alors
 sous forme discrete 
\begin_inset Formula \[
r_{l+1/2}p_{i+1/2}^{2}\frac{f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k+1\right)}-f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)\left(k\right)}}{\Delta t}+r_{l+1/2}\sum_{i^{\prime}=i-1}^{i^{\prime}=i+1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=j-1}^{j^{\prime}=j+1}\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i^{\prime}+1/2,j^{\prime}+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}f_{0,i^{\prime}+1/2,j^{\prime}+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}=0\]

\end_inset 

, les coefficients de la matrice valant 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i+3/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)} & = & \frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{p\xi,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i+1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)} & = & \frac{p_{i+1}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{p\xi,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{p\xi,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & -\frac{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}\Delta\xi_{0j+1}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}D_{\xi\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & -p_{i+1/2}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\right)\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}F_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i-1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)} & = & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{p\xi,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1}+\Delta\xi_{0j}}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\overline{\overline{M}}_{p,i+3/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)} & = & -\frac{p_{i+1}^{2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}\Delta p_{i+1/2}}D_{pp,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}}{\Delta p_{i+1}+\Delta p_{i}}\frac{\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j}^{2}}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}D_{\xi p,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1}^{2}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\left(1-\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\right)F_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

